{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "World of Squares",
    "steam_appid": 3147260,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is the <strong>alpha</strong> release for World of Squares, a cute social MMO to relax and immerse in. You can pet foxes (and fox-morphed players) with your mouse cursor! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fishing, particle physics, painting, parkour, playing music, cooking, fighting \u2014 a plethora of game systems combine together to form limitless possibilities.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Add your friends and chat with them online or offline. Emotes let you express yourself to your friends. Hang out together or enjoy each others' presence in an adorable world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start by choosing your favorite color for your character!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On ensuring your enjoyment:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- This game exists for your enjoyment and health \u2014 a monthly price of a $5 coffee unlocks all content, keeps the servers running, the developer alive, and ensures that the relationship between the game and its players is strictly symbiotic! Game progress, cosmetics, and stash-slots are strictly an in-game fun experience; they <i>cannot</i> be purchased with real world money.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- This is a social game. You can still log in, move around the world, and message your friends even if you can't afford membership. Exactly the extent of free-to-play content is to be determined, but that much is the philosophy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- To me, it feels strange to commit time to an MMO if I know my progress is on someone else's server. I promise I will release a playable local version in a timely manner that has all of your progress if the game must go down and stay down (I won't be alive forever, or perhaps the player-base supporting the servers moves on)</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is the <strong>alpha</strong> release for World of Squares, a cute social MMO to relax and immerse in. You can pet foxes (and fox-morphed players) with your mouse cursor! </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fishing, particle physics, painting, parkour, playing music, cooking, fighting \u2014 a plethora of game systems combine together to form limitless possibilities.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Add your friends and chat with them online or offline. Emotes let you express yourself to your friends. Hang out together or enjoy each others' presence in an adorable world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Start by choosing your favorite color for your character!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On ensuring your enjoyment:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- This game exists for your enjoyment and health \u2014 a monthly price of a $5 coffee unlocks all content, keeps the servers running, the developer alive, and ensures that the relationship between the game and its players is strictly symbiotic! Game progress, cosmetics, and stash-slots are strictly an in-game fun experience; they <i>cannot</i> be purchased with real world money.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- This is a social game. You can still log in, move around the world, and message your friends even if you can't afford membership. Exactly the extent of free-to-play content is to be determined, but that much is the philosophy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- To me, it feels strange to commit time to an MMO if I know my progress is on someone else's server. I promise I will release a playable local version in a timely manner that has all of your progress if the game must go down and stay down (I won't be alive forever, or perhaps the player-base supporting the servers moves on)</p>",
    "short_description": "A feel-good MMO with rich mechanics. Paint with your friends, play a cube violin in the woods, discover an ancient ruins, fight valiant knights and dangerous mobs, become a fox sacrificing yourself to a dangerous altar at midnight, chill with a fishing rhythm game, upgrade your gear and character.",
